:17,"105":16,"106":62,"107":71,"108":116,"109":90,"110":6,"111":82,"112":100,"113":99,"114":87,"115":129,"116":60,"117":102,"118":121,"119":46,"120":38,"121":42,"122":118,"123":125,"124":123,"125":69,"126":120,"127":86,"128":131,"129":57,"130":56,"131":58,"132":4},"orderedDocs":[[28,"_Source: `CHANGELOG.md`_"],[20,"_Source: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`_"],[46,"_Source: `docs/GOALS.md`_"],[58,"_Source: `docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md`_"],[132,"_Source: `docs/TESTING-GUIDE.md`_"],[53,"_Source: `README.md`_"],[110,"_Source: `ROADMAP.md`_"],[93,"[ ] **Accessibility & i18n pass**: keyboard navigation for pins, focus states, screen-reader labels, number/currency formatting."],[84,"[ ] **Auto-orient captures**: detect the ground plane / longest horizontal axis so a scanned bike stands upright facing +X; expose rotate/scale/offset controls in Edit mode (writes `model.rotation/scale/offset`)."],[73,"[ ] **Auto-publish on develop**: a workflow (`contents: write`) that runs `tools/publish-pages.sh --source develop` on every push to `develop`, so the site stays current even when no agent session runs."],[91,"[ ] **Branding**: shop logo, accent color and font in scene settings; applied to Present mode."],[95,"[ ] **Capture guidance for bikes**: checklist overlay (3 orbits: hub height, saddle height, top-down; close-ups of fork crown, dropouts, rear derailleur, cockpit), shot counter per pass, tips for reflective paint (dulling spray / polarizer), turntable support."],[99,"[ ] **Catalog page**: list of bikes (cards with turntable thumbnails), search/filter, each opening its scene."],[101,"[ ] **Collaborative comments**: multiple staff editing comments; history."],[88,"[ ] **Comment polish**: leader lines from pin to card in Present mode, auto-advance/kiosk mode, comment ordering (drag to reorder), markdown-lite (bold, bullet lists) in bodies."],[85,"[ ] **Crop box for area-mode / splat captures**: draggable box in Edit mode that clips everything outside (clipping planes), saved in the scene, so area-mode scans get a clean background."],[105,"[ ] **Docs**: end-to-end guide with screenshots: capture → build → export → annotate → share."],[104,"[ ] **E2E tests**: Playwright smoke test (load demo, fly to Fork, add comment, export JSON) in CI."],[102,"[ ] **Gaussian splat support**: load `.spz` / splat `.ply` (Scaniverse, Polycam, Luma) via Spark (`@sparkjsdev/spark`) for photoreal paint and chrome; crop box + pins work the same."],[89,"[ ] **Hotspot auto-suggest**: for captures, propose default areas (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit, Wheels, Saddle) by letting the user tap each part once; camera view computed from tapped point + local bounds."],[94,"[ ] **In-app viewer**: RealityKit/SceneKit view of `model.usdz` with the same areas and comments (read `bike-scene/1` JSON), so sales staff can present from the phone offline."],[82,"[ ] **Keep captures across reloads**: cache the unzipped model of the last opened bundles in IndexedDB/OPFS (best effort, quota-aware) so a reload reopens a capture scene without re-dropping the `.bikecapture.zip`."],[96,"[ ] **Mac high-detail reconstruction**: `tools/mac-reconstruct` Swift CLI running `PhotogrammetrySession` at `.full` / `.raw` detail from an exported bundle, writing `model.usdz` + `poses.json` back."],[97,"[ ] **On-device GLB export**: convert the USDZ to GLB (ModelIO → glTF writer) so the web viewer never needs conversion."],[103,"[ ] **Performance**: Draco/Meshopt compression, KTX2 textures, lazy loading, 60 fps on iPhone Safari with 50 pins."],[86,"[ ] **Photo close-ups per area**: use `poses.json` to find the capture photos that look most directly at each area target (angle + distance score) and show them as a filmstrip under the area; tap to open full screen. HEIC → JPEG conversion at export time on iOS if browsers can't decode HEIC."],[74,"[ ] **PR previews**: publish each open stack PR under `/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (docs + viewer) and link them from the Progress page, so the owner can test a PR before merging it."],[87,"[ ] **Shareable read-only link**: `?scene=` URL loads a published scene in Present mode with editing hidden; \"Copy share link\" button. Scenes + models served from `apps/web/public/scenes/<id>/`."],[92,"[ ] **Snapshot / video export**: high-res PNG with transparent or green background; 360° turntable WebM via MediaRecorder for social posts."],[90,"[ ] **Spec sheet**: per-bike key specs table (frame material, groupset, weight, sizes) shown in Present mode intro and exported."],[100,"[ ] **Storage**: decide (Cloudflare R2 + Workers, or Supabase) and document; upload bundles, store scenes, auth for editors, public read for shared links."],[98,"[ ] **Upload to viewer**: share sheet target / direct upload of bundles to the web app storage (see Milestone 5)."],[83,"[ ] **USDZ robustness**: verify three.js `USDZLoader` against an Object Capture USDZ (binary USDC inside). If unsupported, document and add `tools/usdz-to-glb.py` (Blender headless) plus a clear in-app message. Add a small sample USDZ fixture if licensing allows (generate one, never commit customer captures)."],[81,"[x] **Capture bundle import**: drop `*.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer, unzip in the browser (fflate), load `model.usdz`, read `manifest.json` and `poses.json`, name the scene from the manifest. Unit-test the bundle parser with a synthetic zip."],[72,"[x] **Docs & progress site**: Fumadocs static site (`apps/docs`) generated from the repo's markdown, with a roadmap progress dashboard and a \"How to test\" guide, published with the viewer to GitHub Pages by `tools/publish-pages.sh` (site at `/bike-3d-brew/`, viewer at `/bike-3d-brew/app/`)."],[49,"**`apps/ios`**: iPhone capture app (Apple Object Capture: background removed automatically, on-device 3D build, camera poses, shareable bundle)."],[50,"**`apps/web`**: three.js viewer and editor: clear / chroma-green / studio backgrounds, fly-to areas, comment pins, presentation mode, JSON export."],[35,"**Capture → viewer in under 15 minutes** with no desktop software: capture on iPhone,\nAirDrop the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer."],[120,"**Edit**: tap the bike to drop a comment pin; save the current camera as a new area."],[37,"**Fast on phones**: first model visible in < 3 s on iPhone Safari over 4G for a 20 MB model;\n60 fps orbiting with 50 pins."],[57,"**GitHub Pages**: done by the owner on 2026-10-27 (Settings → Pages → Deploy from branch\n`gh-pages`). The site is published from this repo by `tools/publish-pages.sh`."],[36,"**Looks like the real bike**: textures, thin parts (spokes, cables) acceptable; background gone."],[121,"**Present**: steps through the areas one by one, as you would with a customer."],[56,"**Real iPhone capture test** (needs an iPhone with LiDAR, iOS 18+): build `apps/ios`, capture a\nbike, export the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer. Report whether the USDZ loads."],[39,"**Robust**: untrusted files never crash the app; every failure says what to do next."],[38,"**Selling tool, not a 3D toy**: areas and comments are the primary UI; present mode is\nusable by a non-technical salesperson with one hand."],[119,"**View**: drag to orbit, pinch to zoom, tap an area chip (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit…) to fly there."],[4,"`bike-capture/1` (iOS export zip)"],[5,"`bike-scene/1` (viewer JSON, `*.bike.json`)"],[41,"`npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run build` and the E2E suite pass; CI green."],[7,"`wesbos/3d-model-anything` records RoomPlan + LiDAR mesh + posed photos, then an AI agent\nrebuilds the room in three.js. A bike is one object with thin tubes, spokes and cables, so we\nuse Apple's Object Capture: guided orbits, **automatic object masking** (the background is\nremoved during reconstruction; no green screen needed) and a textured USDZ. We keep Wes's\nkey idea of **posed photos**: `poses.json` tells us where each photo was taken, so the viewer\ncan show real close-up photos for an area (e.g. the fork crown) next to the 3D view."],[9,"| Path            | Content                                                                                                        |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `manifest.json` | `{ schema, name, createdAt, device, systemVersion, mode: \"object\"\\|\"area\", model, poses, images, imageCount }` |"],[13,"| Path          | Content             |\n| ------------- | ------------------- |\n| `record.json` | app-internal record |"],[11,"| Path         | Content                                                                                              |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `poses.json` | `{ schema: \"bike-poses/1\", samples: [{ sample, file, transform[16] }] }` (column-major camera→model) |"],[10,"| Path         | Content                       |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------- |\n| `model.usdz` | reconstruction, meters, +Y up |"],[12,"| Path      | Content                    |\n| --------- | -------------------------- |\n| `images/` | Object Capture HEIC photos |"],[130,"| PR                       | What to try                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #2 Capture bundle import | **Open…** the synthetic bundle above (or drop it on desktop): it loads and is named from the manifest. Add a comment, reload, open the same file again: the comment is back. |"],[129,"| PR            | What to try                                                                           |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #1 Foundation | Demo bike, areas, comments, Edit and Present modes, background switcher, Export JSON. |"],[131,"| PR        | What to try                                                                     |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docs site | This site: the home page shows roadmap progress; **Progress** lists every item. |"],[34,"A bike shop captures a bike with an iPhone in a few minutes and gets a background-free,\nphotoreal 3D model that sales staff (in store, on a tablet) and customers (on a shared link)\ncan spin, zoom into named areas (fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and read pinned sales comments."],[116,"A short guide for the owner: how to try what the agents built, on a phone or a laptop. Every\nPR that adds something testable extends the \"What each PR adds\" table at the bottom."],[23,"Added"],[106,"AR \"place the bike in your room\" via Quick Look (`model.usdz` + `<a rel=\"ar\">`)."],[1,"Architecture"],[77,"Areas (hotspots) and sales comments pinned to the model surface, edit + present modes"],[19,"Bike size vs. Object Capture's bounding box limits: area mode is the fallback."],[48,"Capture bikes with an iPhone, show them as background-free 3D models, zoom into components\n(fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and pin sales comments on them."],[26,"Capture bundle import: drop an iPhone `*.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer; it is unzipped in the browser, the model loads and the scene is named from the manifest. Re-dropping a bundle restores its comments. (#2)"],[21,"Changelog"],[125,"Checks the agents run on every PR (CI runs them too):"],[80,"CI: web typecheck/test/build, unsigned iOS build on macOS, Pages deploy workflow"],[107,"Compare two bikes side by side."],[3,"Contracts"],[43,"Docs (ROADMAP, CHANGELOG, ARCHITECTURE, guides) updated in the same PR."],[25,"Docs & progress site (Fumadocs, `apps/docs`) generated from the repo's markdown: home dashboard with roadmap progress per milestone, latest changes and build commit; \"How to test\" guide; offline search. `tools/publish-pages.sh` publishes it with the viewer (under `/app/`) and a synthetic test bundle to the `gh-pages` branch; `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` writes a synthetic `*.bikecapture.zip`. The Actions-based `pages.yml` deploy is removed."],[17,"Does `PhotogrammetrySession.Poses` return camera→model transforms in the same frame as the\nUSDZ? (Assumed; validate by projecting a pin into the matching photo.)"],[18,"Does three.js `USDZLoader` read Object Capture USDZ (binary USDC)? Otherwise convert to GLB."],[51,"Drop a `.bikecapture.zip` from the iPhone app (or a `.glb`, `.usdz`, `.ply`) onto the viewer to use your own capture. Switch to **Edit** to\ntap the bike and add comments, save camera views as areas; **Present** steps through areas for\na customer."],[24,"Every PR adds a line under **Unreleased** (newest first) with its PR number. When the owner\nmerges the stack to `main`, the Unreleased block becomes a dated release."],[8,"Fallbacks when Object Capture struggles with a bike (thin spokes are the classic failure):\narea mode + a crop box, or a gaussian splat (Scaniverse/Polycam/Luma) for photoreal paint.\nThe green background mode exists for compositing snapshots/videos in other tools."],[27,"Foundation: three.js viewer/editor with areas, pinned sales comments, present mode, background modes, `bike-scene/1` format; iOS Object Capture app skeleton; CI. (#1)"],[29,"Goals"],[111,"How to test"],[69,"Ideas parking lot"],[14,"Importing in the browser (`apps/web/src/scene/capture.ts`): dropping a `*.bikecapture.zip`\nunzips it in memory with fflate; nothing is uploaded. The iOS exporter zips its staging folder\n(`NSFileCoordinator .forUploading`), so files usually sit under one top-level directory: the\nshallowest `manifest.json` defines the bundle root and `__MACOSX/` / `._*` entries are ignored.\nOnly `manifest.json`, the model and `poses.json` are decompressed (size-capped); images are just\nlisted. If `manifest.model` is missing, a `glb`/`gltf`/`usdz`/`ply` next to the manifest is used\n(GLB first, e.g. after `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`). A broken `poses.json` is a warning, not an error."],[79,"iOS app skeleton: Object Capture (object + area mode), on-device reconstruction, poses, bundle export"],[127,"It writes a low-poly bike as `model.glb`, a `manifest.json`, an orbit of camera poses in\n`poses.json` and no photos, all nested in one folder like the real export. Drag the file onto\nthe viewer (or use **Open…**). Dropping the same file again later restores the comments you\nadded to it."],[114,"Make a synthetic capture bundle"],[54,"Manual steps"],[71,"Markers: `[ ]` open · `[~]` in progress (draft PR open) · `[x]` done (in an open or merged PR)."],[109,"Measure tool (tap two points → distance in mm)."],[62,"Milestone 0: Project ops"],[63,"Milestone 1: Foundation (PR 1)"],[64,"Milestone 2: Real captures into the viewer"],[65,"Milestone 3: Sales experience"],[66,"Milestone 4: iOS app depth"],[67,"Milestone 5: Backend & multi-bike catalog"],[68,"Milestone 6: Quality"],[33,"Non-goals (for now)"],[113,"On a laptop"],[112,"On your phone (no setup)"],[6,"Open questions (verify on device)"],[117,"Open the live demo: **https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/**\n(this site lives one level up: https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/)."],[47,"Overview"],[78,"Procedural demo bike with seeded areas and comments"],[30,"Product"],[59,"Progress"],[44,"Public release / app store distribution (the owner decides when)."],[40,"Pure logic in `apps/web/src/scene/` with unit tests; coverage does not go down."],[32,"Quality bar for every PR"],[45,"Real customer captures in the repo: only generated fixtures."],[61,"Roadmap"],[60,"Roadmap status per milestone, generated from ROADMAP.md at build time."],[76,"Scene format `bike-scene/1` with validation, local persistence, import/export"],[16,"See `apps/web/src/scene/schema.ts`. A scene references its model by URL (relative to the\nscene file), lists **hotspots** (named camera views: the zoomable areas) and **annotations**\n(surface point + normal, title, body, kind `feature|spec|upgrade|note`, optional price and area).\nAll coordinates are in model-root space."],[52,"See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, ROADMAP.md and\napps/ios/README.md. Inspired by\nwesbos/3d-model-anything."],[108,"Size guide overlay (rider silhouette to scale)."],[31,"Success criteria"],[122,"The background buttons switch between clear, chroma green, studio and dark."],[70,"The backlog autonomous sessions work through, top to bottom. Each item is sized for one\nsession / one PR. Protocol is in CLAUDE.md."],[126,"The iPhone app exports `*.bikecapture.zip` (format `bike-capture/1`, see\nArchitecture). To test the import path without a phone:"],[118,"The procedural demo bike loads with sample areas and comments."],[15,"The resulting scene gets a stable id (`capture-<name>-<createdAt digits>`) so dropping the same\nbundle again restores its saved areas and comments, and a model URL `bundle:<zip name>/<path>`,\nwhich is never fetched: after a reload the viewer asks for that zip to be dropped again."],[124,"The site is redeployed by `tools/publish-pages.sh` after each finished PR, so it shows the\nnewest work in the stack, which may not be merged yet. The footer of the home page says which\ncommit and branch it was built from."],[55,"Things an agent cannot do (hardware, accounts, decisions). Newest first."],[123,"To try a capture bundle without the iPhone app, download the synthetic one:\n**https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/samples/synthetic-bike.bikecapture.zip**,\nthen in the viewer tap **Open…** and pick it from Files. A red low-poly bike replaces the demo\nand the scene is named \"Synthetic test bike\"."],[42,"UI changes verified in Chromium with screenshots, at desktop and phone sizes."],[22,"Unreleased"],[75,"Web viewer: three.js, orbit, fly-to areas, background modes (clear / chroma green / studio / 